{
  "name": "03 - Smart Gmail Attachment Filing",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 03 - Smart Gmail Attachment Filing\n**Flow:** Gmail (new email with attachments) -> Config -> split attachments -> filter by type/size -> extract text (PDF text / image vision) -> AI names and classifies -> build YYYY-MM-DD_company_docType_title.ext -> find or create YYYY-MM/docType folders in Drive -> upload (adds _2, _3 on duplicates) -> log to Google Sheets -> label email \"saved-to-drive\" -> Telegram summary.\n\n**Credentials:** Gmail OAuth2, Google Drive OAuth2, Google Sheets OAuth2, OpenAI API, Telegram Bot API.\n\n**Set up:** open the \"Config\" node and fill telegramChatId. Then pick the Drive root folder from the dropdown in \"Search Month Folder\" and \"Create Month Folder\", and the spreadsheet and sheet tab in \"Log File\". The log sheet needs headers: Date, Sender, Subject, Original Name, New Name, Type, Link.\n\n**Test:** run from \"Manual Trigger (Test)\" - it reads up to 3 recent emails matching the query.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 640
      },
      "id": "f2820374-20c0-4c14-ae0c-2c1832767b00",
      "name": "Flow Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -720,
        -16
      ]
    },
    {
